{%- comment -%}
  Bed Finder — static section, rendered once on every page by layout/theme.liquid
  ({% section 'bed-finder' %}, section id "bed-finder").

  Why it exists (choice architecture): a wall of similar beds paralyses. Four
  taps — how the dog sleeps, how their joints are, how big they are, their
  name — end on ONE bed in the right size, addable from the result.

  What it renders
    1. <script type="application/json" id="finder-config"> — what the client
       needs up front: step copy, size hints and the merchant's Match blocks
       with their beds' data. The <bed-finder> element renders its UI from
       this island, so the same component works in the modal, inline on the
       dedicated page (main-finder-page) and when resumed from the teaser.
    2. <template id="finder-icons"> — the theme's own icons, cloned by finder.js.
    3. <template id="finder-notify"> — only while the store has no products:
       "We're not quite open yet" with a launch email sign-up, shown instead of
       the questions (a quiz that can't end on a bed is a dead end).
    4. <dialog class="modal finder-modal"> holding <bed-finder mode="modal">,
       opened by `lunova:finder:open`. Not rendered on the dedicated finder
       page, where the inline finder answers that event instead.
    5. In the theme editor only: a setup panel listing every Match block with
       warnings (no style ticked, unknown sizes, sold out…).

  Matching (finder.js): strict Match blocks first (priority, then order) →
  fallback candidates scored by tags finder:curl|lean|sprawl and
  finder:fine|slowing|diagnosed (+ orthopaedic / memory foam in title or tags)
  → blocks that match on style or stage only. The size is resolved per bed
  from its size option; if that size is sold out the next size up is offered,
  and the result says so.

  Fallback beds are NOT printed here: when some style × stage pair isn't
  covered by an available, all-sizes Match block, the island carries the
  fallback collection's URL and finder.js fetches sections/finder-products
  (Section Rendering API) once a shopper heads for the finder. Products
  tagged finder:exclude and gift cards are never fallback candidates.

  On the bed-finder page template, main-finder-page has already loaded
  finder.css and finder.js, so they aren't requested twice.

  Renders nothing when Theme settings → Bed Finder is switched off.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- if settings.finder_enable -%}
  {%- unless template.suffix == 'bed-finder' -%}
    {{ 'finder.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}
    <script src="{{ 'finder.js' | asset_url }}" defer="defer"></script>
  {%- endunless -%}
  {%- render 'section-styles', section: section -%}

  {%- liquid
    assign cs = section.settings.color_scheme | default: 'bone'
    assign show_modal = true
    if template.suffix == 'bed-finder'
      assign show_modal = false
    endif

    assign fb_coll = section.settings.fallback_collection
    if fb_coll == blank
      assign fb_coll = collections.all
    endif

    comment
      Is every style × stage pair covered by an available Match block that
      takes every size? If so, fallback candidates are never needed.
    endcomment
    assign style_keys = 'curl,lean,sprawl' | split: ','
    assign stage_keys = 'fine,slowing,diagnosed' | split: ','
    assign need_fallback = false
    for st in style_keys
      for sg in stage_keys
        assign covered = false
        assign sk = 'style_' | append: st
        assign gk = 'stage_' | append: sg
        for block in section.blocks
          if block.type != 'match'
            continue
          endif
          assign bp = block.settings.product
          if bp == blank or bp.available != true
            continue
          endif
          assign bsizes = block.settings.sizes | default: '' | strip
          if bsizes != ''
            continue
          endif
          if block.settings[sk] and block.settings[gk]
            assign covered = true
            break
          endif
        endfor
        unless covered
          assign need_fallback = true
        endunless
      endfor
    endfor

    comment
      Fallback beds are fetched on demand (sections/finder-products), and
      only when the fallback collection has anything in it.
    endcomment
    assign fb_count = fb_coll.products_count | default: 0 | plus: 0
    if fb_count > 50
      assign fb_count = 50
    endif
    assign fallback_url = nil
    if need_fallback and fb_count > 0
      assign fallback_url = fb_coll.url
    endif

    comment
      A brand-new store with nothing to sell: the finder offers a launch
      sign-up instead of four questions that can only end on "nothing yet".
    endcomment
    assign shop_total = collections.all.products_count | default: 0 | plus: 0
    assign store_empty = false
    if shop_total == 0
      assign store_empty = true
    endif

    capture hints_json
      render 'size-hints', mode: 'json'
    endcapture
    assign hints_json = hints_json | strip
    if hints_json == ''
      assign hints_json = '[]'
    endif

    assign finder_page_url = routes.root_url | append: '/pages/bed-finder' | replace: '//', '/'

    assign string_keys = 'dialog_label,close,back,next,step_of,your_match,browse_all,your_dog,options.curl_title,options.curl_text,options.curl_short,options.curl_phrase,options.lean_title,options.lean_text,options.lean_short,options.lean_phrase,options.sprawl_title,options.sprawl_text,options.sprawl_short,options.sprawl_phrase,options.fine_title,options.fine_text,options.fine_short,options.slowing_title,options.slowing_text,options.slowing_short,options.diagnosed_title,options.diagnosed_text,options.diagnosed_short,size.meta,size.measure_icon_label,name.label,name.placeholder,name.submit,name.submit_named,name.skip,name.privacy,matching.heading,matching.heading_named,matching.style,matching.stage,matching.size' | split: ','
    assign result_keys = 'heading,heading_named,answers,change,why_heading,why_heading_named,why_style,why_style_miss,material_both,material_foam,material_ortho,why_ortho_diagnosed,why_ortho_slowing,why_ortho_fine,why_fine,why_slowing,why_diagnosed,why_size,why_size_plain,why_size_label,why_size_larger_sold,why_size_larger_missing,why_size_approx,why_size_one,why_trial,vet_note,size_line,size_one,stock_in,stock_low,stock_low_one,stock_backorder,per_night,per_night_basis,per_night_hint,was,now,save,rating,rating_count,add,add_named,add_short_named,add_price,mini_trial,adding,add_error,details,alt_heading,alt_line,alt_switch,alt_view,alt_view_label,diff_cheaper,diff_support,diff_curl,diff_lean,diff_sprawl,diff_other,restart,empty_heading,empty_text,nofit_heading,nofit_text,try_size,setup_note' | split: ','
  -%}

  {%- comment -%} ---------------- 1. Config island ---------------- {%- endcomment -%}
  <script type="application/json" id="finder-config">
    {
      "v": 1,
      "sectionId": {{ section.id | json }},
      "designMode": {{ request.design_mode | json }},
      "urls": {
        "allProducts": {{ routes.all_products_collection_url | json }},
        "finderPage": {{ finder_page_url | json }},
        "cart": {{ routes.cart_url | json }}
      },
      "copy": {
        "styleHeading": {{ section.settings.style_heading | default: '' | json }},
        "styleText": {{ section.settings.style_text | default: '' | json }},
        "stageHeading": {{ section.settings.stage_heading | default: '' | json }},
        "stageText": {{ section.settings.stage_text | default: '' | json }},
        "sizeHeading": {{ section.settings.size_heading | default: '' | json }},
        "sizeText": {{ section.settings.size_text | default: '' | json }},
        "measureTitle": {{ section.settings.measure_title | default: '' | json }},
        "measureText": {{ section.settings.measure_text | default: '' | json }},
        "nameHeading": {{ section.settings.name_heading | default: '' | json }},
        "nameText": {{ section.settings.name_text | default: '' | json }},
        "resultEyebrow": {{ section.settings.result_eyebrow | default: '' | json }},
        "riskText": {{ section.settings.risk_text | default: '' | json }},
        "guaranteeText": {{ section.settings.guarantee_text | default: '' | json }}
      },
      "options": {
        "showAlternative": {{ section.settings.show_alternative | json }},
        "showDelivery": {{ section.settings.show_delivery | json }},
        "showPerNight": {{ section.settings.show_per_night | json }},
        "showRating": {{ settings.show_product_ratings | json }},
        "matchingMoment": {{ section.settings.matching_moment | json }}
      },
      "strings": {
        {%- for k in string_keys -%}
          {%- assign full = 'finder.' | append: k -%}
          {{ k | json }}: {{ full | t | json }},
        {%- endfor -%}
        {%- for k in result_keys -%}
          {%- assign full = 'finder.result.' | append: k -%}
          {%- assign jk = 'result.' | append: k -%}
          {{ jk | json }}: {{ full | t | json }}{%- unless forloop.last -%},{%- endunless -%}
        {%- endfor -%}
      },
      "sizeHints": {{ hints_json }},
      "storeEmpty": {{ store_empty | json }},
      "fallbackUrl": {{ fallback_url | json }},
      "products": {
        {%- assign emitted = '|' -%}
        {%- assign first_p = true -%}
        {%- for block in section.blocks -%}
          {%- liquid
            if block.type != 'match'
              continue
            endif
            assign p = block.settings.product
            if p == blank
              continue
            endif
            assign key = '|' | append: p.handle | append: '|'
            if emitted contains key
              continue
            endif
            assign emitted = emitted | append: p.handle | append: '|'
          -%}
          {%- unless first_p -%},{%- endunless -%}
          {%- assign first_p = false -%}
          {%- render 'finder-product-json', p: p -%}
        {%- endfor -%}
      },
      "matches": [
        {%- assign first_m = true -%}
        {%- for block in section.blocks -%}
          {%- liquid
            if block.type != 'match'
              continue
            endif
            assign bp = block.settings.product
            if bp == blank
              continue
            endif
            assign b_styles = ''
            for st in style_keys
              assign sk = 'style_' | append: st
              if block.settings[sk]
                assign b_styles = b_styles | append: st | append: ','
              endif
            endfor
            assign b_stages = ''
            for sg in stage_keys
              assign gk = 'stage_' | append: sg
              if block.settings[gk]
                assign b_stages = b_stages | append: sg | append: ','
              endif
            endfor
            assign b_styles_arr = b_styles | split: ','
            assign b_stages_arr = b_stages | split: ','
          -%}
          {%- unless first_m -%},{%- endunless -%}
          {%- assign first_m = false -%}
          {
            "block": {{ block.id | json }},
            "handle": {{ bp.handle | json }},
            "styles": {{ b_styles_arr | json }},
            "stages": {{ b_stages_arr | json }},
            "sizes": {{ block.settings.sizes | default: '' | json }},
            "reason": {{ block.settings.reason | default: '' | json }},
            "difference": {{ block.settings.difference | default: '' | json }},
            "priority": {{ block.settings.priority | default: 5 | json }}
          }
        {%- endfor -%}
      ]
    }
  </script>

  {%- comment -%} ---------------- 2. Icons for finder.js ---------------- {%- endcomment -%}
  <template id="finder-icons">
    {%- assign icon_names = 'check,check-circle,arrow-left,arrow-right,chevron-down,close,truck,shield,moon,info,ruler,paw,return,bed,clock,basket' | split: ',' -%}
    {%- for n in icon_names -%}
      <span data-icon="{{ n }}">{%- render 'icon', name: n -%}</span>
    {%- endfor -%}
  </template>

  {%- comment -%}
    ---------------- 3. Launch sign-up (store with no products yet) ----------------
    A plain Shopify customer form: it posts, the page reloads with
    form.posted_successfully?, and finder.js re-opens the finder on the
    "done" state (only after a sign-up made here; see finder.js). Tags let
    the merchant email exactly these people when the beds are in.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- if store_empty -%}
    <template id="finder-notify">
      {%- form 'customer', id: 'FinderNotify', class: 'finder-notify' -%}
        <input type="hidden" name="contact[tags]" value="newsletter,launch-waitlist">
        {%- if form.posted_successfully? -%}
          <div class="finder-result finder-result--empty finder-notify__state" data-notify-state="done" role="status">
            <span class="finder-matching__halo finder-notify__halo" aria-hidden="true">{%- render 'icon', name: 'check' -%}</span>
            <h2 class="finder__heading h3" tabindex="-1" data-step-heading>{{ 'finder.notify.done' | t }}</h2>
          </div>
        {%- else -%}
          <div class="finder-result finder-result--empty finder-notify__state" data-notify-state="{% if form.errors %}error{% else %}form{% endif %}">
            <span class="finder-matching__halo" aria-hidden="true">{%- render 'icon', name: 'paw' -%}</span>
            <h2 class="finder__heading h3" tabindex="-1" data-step-heading>{{ 'finder.notify.heading' | t }}</h2>
            <p class="finder__sub">{{ 'finder.notify.text' | t }}</p>
            <div class="field finder-notify__field">
              <label class="field__label" for="FinderNotifyEmail">{{ 'finder.notify.email_label' | t }}</label>
              <div class="finder-notify__row">
                <input
                  class="input finder-notify__input"
                  id="FinderNotifyEmail"
                  type="email"
                  name="contact[email]"
                  value="{{ form.email | escape }}"
                  autocomplete="email"
                  autocapitalize="off"
                  spellcheck="false"
                  required
                  placeholder="{{ 'finder.notify.placeholder' | t }}"
                  {%- if form.errors %} aria-invalid="true" aria-describedby="FinderNotifyError"{% endif %}
                >
                <button type="submit" class="btn finder-btn-ink finder-notify__submit">{{ 'finder.notify.submit' | t }}</button>
              </div>
              {%- if form.errors -%}
                <p class="field__error finder-notify__error" id="FinderNotifyError" role="alert">{{ 'finder.notify.error' | t }}</p>
              {%- endif -%}
            </div>
          </div>
        {%- endif -%}
      {%- endform -%}
    </template>
  {%- endif -%}

  {%- comment -%} ---------------- 4. The modal ---------------- {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- if show_modal -%}
    <dialog
      class="modal modal--sheet finder-modal scheme-{{ cs }}"
      id="bed-finder"
      aria-label="{{ 'finder.dialog_label' | t }}"
      data-finder-modal
    >
      {%- if request.design_mode -%}
        {%- comment -%} 5. Editor-only setup panel. Each block's root carries shopify_attributes. {%- endcomment -%}
        <details class="finder-setup" open>
          <summary class="finder-setup__summary">{{ 'finder.setup.heading' | t }}</summary>
          <div class="finder-setup__body">
            <p class="finder-setup__intro">{{ 'finder.setup.intro' | t }}</p>
            {%- liquid
              assign hint_tokens = '|'
              assign raw_hints = settings.size_hints | default: '' | newline_to_br | split: '<br />'
              for line in raw_hints
                assign parts = line | strip | split: '|'
                assign hv = parts[0] | default: '' | strip | downcase
                assign hl = parts[1] | default: '' | strip | downcase
                if hv != ''
                  assign hint_tokens = hint_tokens | append: hv | append: '|' | append: hl | append: '|'
                endif
              endfor
              assign hint_tokens = hint_tokens | append: '2xl|xxl|3xl|xxxl|'
            -%}
            <p class="finder-setup__label">{{ 'finder.setup.blocks' | t }}</p>
            {%- if section.blocks.size == 0 -%}
              <p class="finder-setup__empty">{{ 'finder.setup.none' | t }}</p>
            {%- else -%}
              <ol class="finder-setup__list" role="list">
                {%- for block in section.blocks -%}
                  {%- liquid
                    assign bp = block.settings.product
                    assign warns = ''
                    if bp == blank
                      assign w = 'finder.setup.warn_product' | t
                      assign warns = warns | append: w | append: '||'
                    elsif bp.available != true
                      assign w = 'finder.setup.warn_unavailable' | t
                      assign warns = warns | append: w | append: '||'
                    endif
                    unless block.settings.style_curl or block.settings.style_lean or block.settings.style_sprawl
                      assign w = 'finder.setup.warn_style' | t
                      assign warns = warns | append: w | append: '||'
                    endunless
                    unless block.settings.stage_fine or block.settings.stage_slowing or block.settings.stage_diagnosed
                      assign w = 'finder.setup.warn_stage' | t
                      assign warns = warns | append: w | append: '||'
                    endunless
                    assign bad_sizes = ''
                    assign size_list = block.settings.sizes | default: '' | split: ','
                    for s in size_list
                      assign sv = s | strip | downcase
                      if sv == ''
                        continue
                      endif
                      assign needle = '|' | append: sv | append: '|'
                      unless hint_tokens contains needle
                        if bad_sizes != ''
                          assign bad_sizes = bad_sizes | append: ', '
                        endif
                        assign bad_sizes = bad_sizes | append: s | strip
                      endunless
                    endfor
                    if bad_sizes != ''
                      assign bad_esc = bad_sizes | escape
                      assign w = 'finder.setup.warn_sizes' | t | replace: '[sizes]', bad_esc
                      assign warns = warns | append: w | append: '||'
                    endif
                    assign b_flags = ''
                    for st in style_keys
                      assign sk = 'style_' | append: st
                      if block.settings[sk]
                        assign lk = 'finder.options.' | append: st | append: '_short'
                        assign lbl = lk | t
                        assign b_flags = b_flags | append: lbl | append: ' · '
                      endif
                    endfor
                    for sg in stage_keys
                      assign gk = 'stage_' | append: sg
                      if block.settings[gk]
                        assign lk = 'finder.options.' | append: sg | append: '_short'
                        assign lbl = lk | t
                        assign b_flags = b_flags | append: lbl | append: ' · '
                      endif
                    endfor
                    assign size_txt = block.settings.sizes | default: '' | strip
                    if size_txt == ''
                      assign size_txt = 'finder.setup.all_sizes' | t
                    endif
                    assign warn_list = warns | split: '||'
                  -%}
                  <li class="finder-setup__item{% if warn_list.size > 0 %} has-warning{% endif %}" {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>
                    <span class="finder-setup__title">{% if bp != blank %}{{ bp.title | escape }}{% else %}—{% endif %}</span>
                    <span class="finder-setup__meta">{{ b_flags | escape }}{{ size_txt | escape }} · {{ 'finder.setup.priority' | t | replace: '[n]', block.settings.priority }}</span>
                    {%- for w in warn_list -%}
                      <span class="finder-setup__warn">{{ w }}</span>
                    {%- endfor -%}
                  </li>
                {%- endfor -%}
              </ol>
            {%- endif -%}
            <p class="finder-setup__label">
              {%- if need_fallback -%}
                {%- assign fb_title = fb_coll.title | default: '' | escape -%}
                {{ 'finder.setup.fallback' | t | replace: '[count]', fb_count | replace: '[collection]', fb_title }}
              {%- else -%}
                {{ 'finder.setup.fallback_skipped' | t }}
              {%- endif -%}
            </p>
            {%- if store_empty -%}
              <p class="finder-setup__empty">{{ 'finder.setup.no_products' | t }}</p>
            {%- endif -%}
          </div>
        </details>
      {%- endif -%}

      <bed-finder class="finder finder--modal" mode="modal" data-section-id="{{ section.id }}">
        <div class="finder__boot">
          <p class="finder__boot-text">{{ 'finder.loading' | t }}</p>
          <a class="btn btn--secondary" href="{{ routes.all_products_collection_url }}">{{ 'finder.browse_all' | t }}</a>
        </div>
      </bed-finder>
    </dialog>
  {%- endif -%}
{%- endif -%}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Bed Finder",
  "class": "section-bed-finder",
  "max_blocks": 30,
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Four taps to one bed in the right size: how the dog sleeps, their joints, their size, their name. Add a Match block for each bed, or tag products finder:curl / finder:lean / finder:sprawl and finder:fine / finder:slowing / finder:diagnosed and the finder chooses for you."
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Question 1 · How they sleep"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "style_heading",
      "label": "Question",
      "default": "How does your dog sleep?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "style_text",
      "label": "Helper text",
      "default": "Think of how you find them at 2am, not how they settle at 9pm."
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Question 2 · Joints"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "stage_heading",
      "label": "Question",
      "default": "How are their joints?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "stage_text",
      "label": "Helper text",
      "default": "This decides how much support they need, so go with what you see day to day."
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Question 3 · Size"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "size_heading",
      "label": "Question",
      "default": "How big are they?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "size_text",
      "label": "Helper text",
      "default": "Pick the breeds closest to yours. No need to know their weight."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "measure_title",
      "label": "Measuring tip title",
      "default": "Between sizes? How to measure"
    },
    {
      "type": "textarea",
      "id": "measure_text",
      "label": "Measuring tip",
      "default": "Wait until they're asleep and stretched out. Measure from nose to the base of the tail, then add 20cm. Between sizes, or a puppy still growing? Go up one: a bed a little too big is fine, one too small isn't."
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Question 4 · Name"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "name_heading",
      "label": "Question",
      "default": "Last thing — what's their name?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "name_text",
      "label": "Helper text",
      "default": "So we can make this about them. You can skip it."
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Result"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "result_eyebrow",
      "label": "Small label above the match",
      "default": "Based on your answers"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "risk_text",
      "label": "Trial line under the button",
      "default": "Sleep on it for [nights] nights. If it isn't right, we collect it free and refund every penny.",
      "info": "[nights] becomes the trial length from Theme settings → Promises. Hidden when the trial is switched off."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "guarantee_text",
      "label": "Guarantee line",
      "default": "Backed by our [years]-year guarantee.",
      "info": "[years] comes from Theme settings → Promises. Hidden when the guarantee is switched off."
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "show_alternative",
      "label": "Show an alternative pick",
      "default": true,
      "info": "A second bed with one clear difference (price, shape or support), so a shopper who doesn't fancy the first has somewhere to go."
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "show_delivery",
      "label": "Show the delivery estimate",
      "default": true,
      "info": "Worked out from your real dispatch cut-off in Theme settings → Promises."
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "show_per_night",
      "label": "Show the per-night cost",
      "default": true,
      "info": "Only shows when Theme settings → Pricing → per-night is on and the guarantee is enabled."
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "matching_moment",
      "label": "Show a short \"finding your bed\" moment",
      "default": true,
      "info": "Under a second, ticking off the three answers that were used. Skipped for anyone who prefers reduced motion."
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "When no Match block fits"
    },
    {
      "type": "collection",
      "id": "fallback_collection",
      "label": "Choose from this collection",
      "info": "Blank uses all products (up to 50). Beds are scored by their finder: tags, and orthopaedic / memory foam in the title or tags. Tag a product finder:exclude to leave it out."
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Pop-up"
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "color_scheme",
      "label": "Colour scheme",
      "options": [
        { "value": "bone", "label": "Bone" },
        { "value": "oat", "label": "Oat" },
        { "value": "white", "label": "White" },
        { "value": "moss", "label": "Moss" }
      ],
      "default": "bone"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "padding_top",
      "label": "Space above questions",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 120,
